    },
    "comment_count": 0,
    "committer": {
     "date": "2026-04-02T16:56:42Z",
     "email": "cpettus@pgexperts.com",
     "name": "Christophe Pettus"
    },
    "message": "Modernize django-pglocks to 2.0\n\n- Replace setup.py/distutils with pyproject.toml and hatchling build backend\n- Move to src/ layout with Python 3.10+ and Django 4.2+ minimum\n- Add async_advisory_lock context manager (sync_to_async-based)\n- Split internals into _lock.py (pure functions), _sync.py, _async.py\n- 64-bit SHA-256 string hashing (breaking change from 32-bit CRC32)\n- Keyword-only arguments for shared, wait, comment, using\n- Parameterized SQL queries instead of string formatting\n- Robust stack-walking for comment feature\n- Proper cursor lifecycle (try/finally)\n- Full test suite: 55 tests (pytest + pytest-django + pytest-asyncio)\n- GitHub Actions CI: lint/mypy/build + 128-combo matrix\n- Docker Compose for contributor setup\n- Type annotations throughout with py.typed (PEP 561)\n- Remove six dependency, Python 2 support, build artifacts\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
